{title: 450 - Beautiful Zion}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #450 • }
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: D}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 450}
{meta: category Early Advent - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[D]Beautiful Zion, [A]built [A7]a[D]bove,
Beautiful [Bm]city [A7]that [D]I [A]love,
[D]Beauti[G]ful [D]gates of [D7]pea[G]rl[A]y [G]white,
Beautiful [Dsus]tem [D][Bm]ple, [D]God [A7]its [D]light.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[D]Beautiful [A]trees [A7]forever [D]there,
[Bm]Beautiful [A7]fruit [D]they [A]always bear,
[D][G]Beautiful [D][D7]rivers [G][A]gliding [G]by,
[Dsus][D]Beautiful [Bm]fountains [D][A7]never [D]dry.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[D]Beautiful [A]crowns [A7]on [D]every brow,
[Bm]Beautiful [A7]palms [D]the [A]conquerors show,
[D][G]Beautiful [D]robes [D7][G]the [A]ransomed [G]wear,
[Dsus][D]Beautiful [Bm]all [D]who [A7]enter [D]there.
{end_of_verse}
